### 2026-10-01 — ns3d-coordnet: one frozen coordinate-network bank for NS 3D at 32³/64³/96³ in the co-moving frame (lane closed)

**Where.** Branch `exp/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank` (sparse worktree `worktrees/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank`, forked from `exp/2026-09-25-t2-ns3d-test` @acf1af87), local only, never pushed; code/results mirrored by `experiments/ns3d-coordnet/sync_github.sh` to `origin/codeonly/exp/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank`. Lane dir `experiments/ns3d-coordnet/` (pre-registration `DESIGN.md` + amendments A1–A4; Codex audits in `results/codex-*.md`). Generated report `reports/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank.md` (from `reports/build_2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank.py`; local to the branch). Namespace `/cluster/tufts/paralab/tawal01/nscoord_20261001/` is empty (every job pulled, checksum-verified, deleted). Framed as a standalone research question (the ICLR paper was discarded by the user the same day; paper_latex not touched).

**Ran.** Bank = curl of a periodic integer-Fourier-feature MLP vector potential (exactly div-free), R=64, trained once by a variable-projection objective on 3072 centred training states pooled over 32/64/96 (seed 202609201), ordered by the paper's QR+SVD rotation, read at mesh n as Löwdin(P_n · sample · T). Jobs (A100 80GB, jax_backend=gpu, f64, precision highest): pilot 4708239 (3 architectures, ~30 min each; arch A kept); fixed-frame control ff64b 4711021; dev32 4713119, dev64 4713141, dev96 4713143 (16 dev cases each, k=8 head per mesh with the shift-head recipe, spans R'=64…8, paper's frozen POD heads as reference arm, CNAB2 ladder, interleaved timing, frame-frozen control, LM parity, in-job NumPy audit incl. an independent floor recomputation); test 4717237 (seed 202609221, 32 cases, all three meshes, settings frozen in `frozen/frozen_settings.json` and committed before submission; opened once for this lane). Never computed: 4711010/11/13/15 (GPU preflight failed on pax007). Cancelled, never evaluated: 4711018/19/20 (10 h production fits, ~25 min in).

**Found (development; test in parentheses).**
- Floor (oracle centroid, evolved worst): coordnet R=64 1.004 / 1.243 / 1.257 % at 32/64/96 vs POD-64 0.125 / 0.129 / 0.129 % (8.1–9.8×). Bar (a) as registered (≤1.5× POD) FAILS; relaxed by user to "accepted at ~1 %". Frozen fit's training loss 5.2e-5 vs its own optimum 3.7e-7 (same-data POD floor 0.142 % at 32³): the gap is the fit.
- Head k=8: 1.022 / 1.253 / 1.267 % (test 1.085 / 1.265 / 1.279 %, 0/32 over 5 %), i.e. 1.01–1.02× its bank floor at every mesh on both cohorts. 96³ speed 5.74× CNAB2 (50 steps) dev, 7.92× (70 steps) test. Bar (b′) (A4: head ≤1.5× floor everywhere + ≥5× CNAB2 at 96³) PASSES; original bar (b) (≤0.25 % at 96³) FAILS.
- Bar (c) FAILS: same bank sha256 in all jobs; head max/min 1.239 (dev, passes ≤1.25; test 1.179); floor max/min 1.252 (misses ≤1.25); pre-Löwdin deviation 1.9e-2 / 1.36e-3 / 1.49e-3 (fails ≤1e-3 everywhere). 64³ and 96³ agree closely (bank columns 1.1 % apart after restriction); the 32³ reading is a different bank (14 % column difference, lower floor) — most likely the network carries detail a 32³ grid cannot resolve (raw autodiff/FFT derivative mismatch 17 % at 32³ → 2 % at 64³). Inference, not tested.
- Derivatives: D_d is the exact spectral derivative of the sampled/projected/Löwdin bank actually used (checks 1e-15 dense, 1.7e-11 shift finite difference at every mesh); autodiff only a diagnostic (on the tests 4.9e-3 / 3.7e-5 / 1.5e-7).
- Controls fire: fixed-frame coordnet bank 70.16 % at every mesh; no-centring 97.6 % (32³); frame-frozen head 40.2–40.4 % dev (≤42.6 % test). POD reference reproduces its earlier jobs to ≤1e-12 (dev) and ≤4.4e-13 (test). Speed comparators recomputed independently by Codex for all 48 rows.

**Wrong / retracted / deviations.** (1) Codex audit pass 1 found the integer Fourier frequencies were trainable (would have broken periodicity silently) — fixed before any job. (2) **Pre-registration deviated by user decision after the pilot (A4)**: the 5 h/10 h production fits (R=64/128/256, band-limit penalty of A3) were cancelled and the 30-min pilot bank frozen; bar (a) relaxed, bar (b) redefined relative to the floor; "R needed to match POD-64" is unanswered. (3) The autodiff-vs-spectral derivative mismatch was first treated as a correctness issue; it is under-resolution (see above) and the frame never used autodiff. (4) Report audit (Codex) made me qualify the aliasing explanation as an inference, distinguish the registration history, and correct "never computed" vs "cancelled". (5) A stray malformed `submit.sh` call before the test job exited before creating any directory or job (squeue showed exactly one test job).

**Open.** A band-limited bank (A3 recipe) is the direct test of whether bar (c)'s 32³ discrepancy is this artifact's aliasing; longer fits / larger ranks for the POD-64 floor gap were never evaluated; a single head shared across meshes untested. Merge decision for the branch not taken (ask the user).

### 2026-10-01/02 — quadrature-burgers3d: Hari's off-mesh quadrature on the full-scale Burgers 3D model (lane closed)

**Where.** Worktree `worktrees/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d`, branch `exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d` (forked from `exp/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank` @21c175a1b; never pushed; mirrored to `origin/codeonly/exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d`). Lane dir `experiments/quadrature-burgers3d/` (DESIGN.md + amendments R1–R5; code offmesh.py, qpanel.py, refjob.py, rules.py, refine_q.py, select_q.py, audit_q.py, npcore.py, make_report.py; vendored frozen model M2 bank sha256 6687f259… and burgers3d-span/retry code). Report `reports/2026-10-01-burgers3d-offmesh-quadrature.md` (generated by make_report.py). Frozen `selection.json` sha256 ca69098a38b4f145178a4612c96bc12d425fe8f53aa47583eef2aaf55e5bf524 (commit 2805fe949, before any held-out job). Namespace `/cluster/tufts/paralab/tawal01/quad3d_20261001/` removed.
**Jobs (10).** smoke1 4731591 (H200; 65-node smoke + 513-node tolerance probe), ref1 4732809 (A100, FAILED GPU preflight, no CUDA device) → ref1 4732869 (H100; 513-node, dt .0025 refined references for 923801×64 and 923901×32), rck1 4733462 (H100; tolerance re-check), val65/129/257 4732813/4732818/4732820 (H200, validation 923801×64), ho65/129/257 4737003/4737005/4737007 (H200, held-out 923901×32). All jax_backend=gpu, f64, highest.
**Setup.** Only the advection term of the frozen R=512 span model is replaced: N^{3/2} Σ w_q ψ(x_q) u (u_x+u_y+u_z)(x_q) with the bank and its analytic (1,1,1)-derivative at the rule points; linear terms, projection and decoding stay mesh-exact; same cached-predictor LM solver (gate G4: identical to the vendor make_fsc). Arms: tensor (incumbent), dense sign-upwind (64³; 4 cases at 128³), CBC lattices 4096/8192/16384/32768, Korobov 16381, Gauss 16³/24³/32³, Sobol 16384; controls lattice-256 and Smolyak level 8. R'∈{512,256}, dt .01.
**Findings (held-out, worst over 32 cases).**
- (i) Lattice beats Gauss at equal m at every mesh/width (continuum ρ, R'=512: 4096 pts 8.3e-2/1.0e-1/1.2e-1 vs Gauss 16³ 0.61–0.62; 32768 pts 0.9–2.0e-4 vs Gauss 32³ 4.7–6.6e-4). Smolyak ρ 24–45, lattice-256 ρ 2–3.4 (both controls fire). A fixed rule's continuum ρ grows with the mesh (sharper reached states): lattice-4096 at R'=512 fails the 0.116 bar at 256³. 4096 lattice points already reach the tensor's refined accuracy everywhere; within 1e-3 of the converged rollout needs 16384 (R'=512, validation) / 4096 (R'=256).
- (ii) Against the 513-node refined reference the off-mesh solve does NOT reproduce the tensor — it is better and mesh-invariant: selected gl24 (R'=512) 2.83 % at 64³/128³/256³ (ratio 1.003; cross-mesh distance 0.072 % → 0.023 %) vs tensor 10.46/6.09/3.87 % (ratio 2.70; 4.6 % → 2.8 %); lat4096 (R'=256) 4.49 % at all meshes vs tensor 10.57/6.56/5.07 %. The tensor tracks the same-mesh FOM's first-order upwind error (best FOM refined 9.85/5.22/2.27 %). Off-mesh vs tensor distance = the O(h) gap (ρ of dense upwind vs continuum 0.195/0.098/0.052). At 64³/128³ no same-mesh FOM setting is as accurate as the off-mesh solve; at 256³ the best FOM (2.27 %) is.
- (iii) Cost: off-mesh query cheaper than the tensor in all six cells (R'=512: 34.1 vs 47.9, 40.6 vs 52.0, 76.7 vs 90.1 ms; R'=256: 11.1 vs 12.2, 12.1 vs 14.1, 33.0 vs 35.1 ms). Memory 0.34 GB (gl24) / 50 MB (lat4096) vs 4.30 GB / 0.54 GB tensor; Jacobian 0.66 vs 1.04 ms despite 29 vs 1.1 GFLOP (GEMM vs bandwidth-bound contraction). At 256³ query time is dominated by mesh projection/decoding. Speedups vs Newton–BiCGStab at 256³: same-grid rule 2.21×→2.59× (R'512), 5.66×→6.01× (R'256); refined rule 2.21×→6.45× (R'512). At 64³ every reduced arm is slower than the FOM. Same-job tensor reproduces the published 256³ row (2.20 %/2.21×, 3.77 %/5.66×).
- (iv) k-head not revisited; nothing retrained.
**Gates/audits.** G1–G4, table, reference, continuum-target check (≤1.2e-7) pass at every panel; timing gates pass (ROM neighbour check untested at 256³: no arm 4× slower than another). NumPy audits pass on all six panels (refined errors in-job vs NumPy ≤2.8e-16; every recorded worst ρ reproduced; fault injections detected). Codex: design audit (4 blockers, fixed in R1), R1 re-check (fixed in R2), results audit (no blockers; majors fixed in the report).
**Wrong / retracted / deviations.** (1) Design audit: vendor FOM would stack all 100 states at 513 nodes (~107 GB) and capture the spectral array; replaced by a lean FOM (gate: identical to vendor at 65 nodes). Selection had an unconditional fallback — removed. (2) ref1 4732809 failed the GPU preflight; restaged unchanged on H100. (3) The smoke probe could not discriminate reference tolerances; R4 re-check found up to 1.02e-5 (one of four cases above the 1e-5 threshold) → reference declared tolerance-limited at ~1e-5 (refined differences <1.0e-4 unresolved; immaterial at the %-level differences reported). (4) Smoke panel timing gates failed (2 cases × 2 reps; diagnostic only). (5) Held-out audits first run with the held-out re-selection check, which "failed" because re-applying the rule to held-out data picks lat8192 instead of the frozen gl24 at R'=512 (lat8192 missed the 1e-3 rollout criterion on validation by 0.02–0.03 pp); that is a stability finding, not an audit failure — audits re-run without it (originals kept in results/superseded/). (6) Richardson estimate u_R = 2u_513 − u_257 added post-hoc after validation (R5), diagnostic only; refined reference itself differs from u_R by up to 2.28 %. (7) Codex results audit: report had a wrong median (47.7→47.1 s), an overstated "all certified rules agree" claim, and an ambiguous speedup sentence — fixed. (8) Held-out cohort 923901 had been evaluated before by the retry lane for its tensor settings (disclosed).
**Open.** The refined reference is first-order; a second-order or finer reference would sharpen the off-mesh vs FOM comparison at 256³. Off-mesh certification should be redone per mesh (ρ grows with mesh). Whether off-mesh advection makes the head trainable/usable (iv) is untested. Worktree not merged — ask the user. Last lane commit aab6b6927, mirror commit 9361e88c3 (origin/codeonly/exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d).

### 2026-10-01/02 — quadrature-study: Hari's off-mesh quadrature on the full-scale Burgers 2D model (lane closed)

**Where.** Worktree `worktrees/2026-10-01-quadrature-study`, branch `exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-study` (forked from `exp/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank` @21c175a1b; branch never pushed; mirrored to `origin/codeonly/exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-study` after every commit). Code/results `experiments/quadrature-study/`; DESIGN.md (pre-registration + amendments A0–A5); report (generated by `reports/make_report.py`, final, test cohort included) `reports/2026-10-01-burgers2d-offmesh-quadrature.md`. Namespace `/cluster/tufts/paralab/tawal01/quad2d_20261001/` emptied and removed; no lane job left.

**Setup.** Frozen Table-1 Burgers 2D model (dn256b, R=512, K=16, rotation_R512); three settings: accurate span R'=384/M=1536, fast span R'=128/M=512, head k=16/q=0/M=64; LM gtol 1e-3 everywhere. Only the tested advection is replaced (the user's hybrid): dense upwind on all nodes, mesh rules (deployed 63² lattice `lat64`; head's fitted NNLS EQ `q0scaled`), or Hari's off-mesh form L Σ w_q ψ(x_q) u(u_x+u_y)(x_q) (and flux form) with the bank + forward-mode gradient at Gauss 32²–256², Fibonacci 1597–46368, Sobol 4096; continuum rollout `gref` = Gauss 640² (certified vs 768² and flux form, G6); controls Smolyak CC 8 and Gauss 8². Refined references at 8192²: ST (dt/16, primary) and S (same dt), on the shared 257² nodes. Cohorts dev6, val32 (= sel32), test64 (reused historical cohort; nothing chosen from it).

**Jobs (9).** refdv 4734273 (A100, 76 refs, all accepted), reft 4734276 (A100, 128 refs, all accepted), fz4096 4735747 (H200, feasibility, 1 dev case), dv256 4735696 / dv1024 4735709 (A100-80G), dv4096 4735717 (H200), t256 4739520 / t1024 4739521 (A100-80G), t4096 4739522 (H200). Every applicable gate passes in every ROM job (G1–G8 incl. parity with the Table-1/Table-2 records to ≤1.3e-13, both controls failing everywhere, NumPy audit of errors ≤1e-10 and ρ ≤1e-6, timed outputs identical to phase 1).

**Found (numbers from the generated report).**
- (i) Linear rungs: resolved off-mesh rules give mesh-invariant errors case by case (largest per-case ST spread over 256²/1024²/4096²: 0.020 pp dev, 0.011 pp test; B2 1.0001–1.0060 on dev). Dense (upwind) improves with the mesh. Matched dev cases, accurate: continuum rollout ST 2.75/2.75/1.82 %, S 1.06/1.05/0.24 % vs dense ST 6.21/3.38/1.91 %, S 4.16/1.34/0.24 % (38/38/6 cases); test: 2.64/2.65/1.57 % and 1.34/1.36/0.10 % vs dense 5.58/3.27/1.62 % and 3.71/1.53/0.10 % (64/64/6). So the off-mesh solve on a coarse mesh is more accurate (cohort-worst) than dense there, and at 4096² the worst errors are close (slightly lower vs ST, slightly higher vs S). Head setting: NOT mesh-invariant on test (B2 1.91; cases 36/48/60 move up to 4.7 pp for every arm, dense and lat64 included) — a head-solve effect, cause not isolated.
- (ii) Our bank converges far more slowly in m than Hari's (Gauss 64², Fibonacci ~4–7k: continuum ρ_max ~1e-2 at the accurate setting; Gauss 128² ~2–7e-3; continuum target needed 640²). At ~4k points: lat64 5.4e-2 vs its mesh target, Gauss 64² 1.9e-2 / Fibonacci 4181 3.3e-2 vs the continuum (dev, 1024², accurate) — different targets. Sobol 4096 ~0.1–0.25, Smolyak 8 up to 9.5 (fail). Deployed lat64 fails B3 at accurate 256²/1024² (0.13 / 0.27 % from dense); fitted head EQ fails B3 at 256²/1024² (0.65 / 0.81 %).
- (iii) Solve time (median query − median decode) is flat in N on one H200: B4 ratios 0.937–1.060 (dev) and 0.972–1.040 (test) for all 40 arms; grows with m. Full query is not flat (decode of six output fields grows with N). At 4096²: accurate Gauss 96² 54.5 ms vs lat64 46.3 ms; fast Fibonacci 1597 13.3 vs 18.7 ms; head Gauss 32² 22.3 vs 40.6 ms (not a matched equal-accuracy comparison).
