     1	"""jcp-robust E2 3D rule selection per (bank, width, spec, family) (DESIGN 3.3; A1.8, A2.5, A2.6, A3.3). CPU (offline first).
     2	
     3	From the two selection jobs of one bank (e2q<b>a: W256, W512; e2q<b>b: W768, W1024; d3run 'ladder' blocks) and their E0
     4	scores: a candidate rung is qualified iff, on every one of the 64 cases, its production run is valid, the pooled
     5	non-stationary fraction (fresh in-job certificate, recomputed from the saved gam_cert rows) is <= 1 %, the ADT tight
     6	anchor is valid and within 2.5e-4 (recomputed), tight/tighter <= 2.5e-5 on cases 0-7, its successor rung is valid and
     7	within 2.5e-4 (recomputed), rho against the successor <= 0.116, and (cross-family) it is within 2.5e-4 of gl64 on every
     8	case. The target check is gl56 vs gl64 <= 2.5e-5 on cases 0-7 with both valid; if it fails, the pick is a diagnostic pick
     9	on the own-family criteria (A2.5). Search order = the candidate lists; three-state: an undetermined candidate stops the
    10	search ("unavailable"); "none within ladder" only when every candidate is definitively rejected.
    11	
    12	    python select3d.py <bank> <e2q<b>a dir> <e2q<b>b dir>
